/// Per-player packet timing for anticheat plugins. Vine times every packet a player sends
/// natively and hands plugins one summary per player per window, so no plugin runs per packet.
/// Needs `[packet_timing] enabled = true` in vine.toml; otherwise `take-packet-timing` is empty.
///
/// Packets are read as the backend gets them (the current version for clients Vine
/// translates). Metric names:
///
/// - `packets`, `packets_per_second_max`: every packet the client sent, and the most in any
///   one second.
/// - `swings`, `cps_max`: arm swings (left clicks), and the most in any one second.
/// - `swing_intervals`, `swing_interval_mean_ms`, `swing_interval_stddev_ms`: gaps between
///   swings under one second apart; mean and deviation only with at least two.
/// - `attacks`, `attacks_per_second_max`: attack packets.
/// - `rotations`, `rotation_snaps`, `rotation_delta_max`: packets carrying a rotation, turns of
///   45 degrees or more in one packet, and the largest turn in degrees.
/// - `moves`, `moves_per_second_max`: movement packets.
/// - `ticks`, `timer_balance_max_ms`: client ticks (tick-end packets from 1.21.2, movement
///   packets up to 1.8, none in between), and how far they ran ahead of real time, ms; the
///   balance only when ticks were seen.
/// - `air_rise_max`, `hover_ms_max`: most height gained in one run off the ground, blocks,
///   and the longest time off the ground without falling, ms, from the client's on-ground flag.
///   Declared flight is skipped; a teleport or switch starts a new run.
///
/// Metric names are snake_case strings so new ones need no interface change.
interface packet-timing {
    /// One player's packet timing over one window.
    record player-packet-timing {
        uuid: string,
        /// The client's real protocol version.
        protocol-version: u32,
        /// How long the window ran, ms.
        window-ms: u64,
        metrics: list<tuple<string, f64>>,
    }

    /// Ends the window for every player and returns it, one entry per player online during it
    /// (players who left since the last call included, once). The next window starts now.
    /// Several plugins calling this share the windows, so one plugin should own it.
    take-packet-timing: func() -> list<player-packet-timing>;
}
